Then answer:
Which metric is most important for your particular problem, and why?
 Recall is the most important for this problem. The cost of a false negative, where the model predicts someone won’t play when they actually will, is generally worse than a false positive, where the model predicts someone will play but they don’t, because missing real demand is more costly than being a little more prepared on a quiet day. 


